From ba272329359b5efb22d19369071310d159233a3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:19:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/19] freedreno/registers: make the 2D blit ifmt enums common

a5xx and a6xx have the same (or similar) 2D blit core, and the enums
describing the intermediate format it converts through are identical:
the same eight values with the same names.  a5xx cannot use them,
though, because they live in a6xx_enums.xml, so fd5_blitter.c carries a
hand-written copy.

Move a6xx_2d_ifmt and a6xx_sp_a2d_output_ifmt_type to adreno_common.xml,
which both generations already import, and rename them to adreno_2d_ifmt
and adreno_2d_output_ifmt_type after the convention there.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45483>

Base-commit: b69adc2adfbfe3eb985bd66cd06c61ca719ae9ae
Apply in filename order within this project.
Upstream-commit: ba272329359b5efb22d19369071310d159233a3a
Source: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/commit/ba272329359b5efb22d19369071310d159233a3a
Backport: refresh the fd6_blitter.cc context around the existing destination-format conversion; retain the A6xx and Turnip enum consumers.

